{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Righteous balances, righteous stones.</b> The meaning is: by weight." "<b>A righteous ephah.</b> For dry measure." "<b>And a righteous hin.</b> For liquid — the meaning is: by measure." "And the sense of <b>I am YHWH your Elohim who brought you out.</b> Because He mentioned that you were strangers in the land of Egypt, therefore you are obligated to keep My statutes and My ordinances in your heart and to do them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:13.447767270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}